idth="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aulic War Council</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aulic War Council, or Hofkriegsrat, was the central military administration of the Habsburg Monarchy, established in Vienna in 1556.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulikara-dynasty"><span class="enc-name">Aulikara dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aulikara dynasty ruled the region of Dashapura, modern Mandsaur in western Malwa, in the fifth and sixth centuries CE, at first as subordinates of the Gupta Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulus-cornelius-cossus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aulus-cornelius-cossus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aulus Cornelius Cossus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aulus Cornelius Cossus was a Roman commander of the 5th century BCE who killed Lars Tolumnius, king of Veii, in single combat during the war over Fidenae.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulus-gabinius"><span class="enc-name">Aulus Gabinius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aulus Gabinius was a Roman politician and general.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulus-plautius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aulus-plautius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aulus Plautius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aulus Plautius was a Roman senator and general who commanded the invasion of Britain ordered by the emperor Claudius in 43 CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aulus-postumius-albinus"><span class="enc-name">Aulus Postumius Albinus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Aulus Postumius Albinus was a Roman